      "note": "This is the drafter's own list of the usual fall-risk medicines: benzodiazepines, zolpidem, antipsychotics, opioids, gabapentin and pregabalin, other antiepileptics, bladder antimuscarinics, promethazine, diuretics, alpha-blockers, nitrates and centrally acting blood pressure medicines. A different antidepressant that raises falls risk can count. Count repeat supplies of one ingredient only once. Count a listed diuretic in a combination tablet. For each medicine, check the active ingredient and form against the product information if uncertain. Generic packs that show the ingredient name with a company name count too."
